                     <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_75357584">32.9x41.6</dimensions>
                     <watermark xml:id="watermark_a9e1c7f4">on fol. 2 the Pro Patria emblem is visible; the paper has the countermark 'C &amp; I H' (C. and J. Honig), most likely same type as bs. part. Paper of a fairly dense quality.</watermark>
                     <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_7baf1096">In 2<rend xml:id="idm89" rend="sup">o</rend>; upright format; music (fols. 1r–2v); in all a single bifolio. Hand-ruled staves, 13 staves (11 mm; single rastrum used) in dark brown ink and music in black ink, with ornaments added in same ink presumably by the same hand; bottom three staves on fol. 2r have not been used. A clean copy.</physMedium>
